Local (budi, 2026-10-11, rev 2): copy-on-write for QSA host K/V.

Symptom: with --prefix-match-unit finer than the QSA block, any prefix-cache
hit that ends inside a block corrupted the output (2026-10-02 echo probe: 9/9
exact without a hit, 0/6 with one). Whole-block hits were fine.

Cause: vLLM serves a partial-block hit by giving the request a fresh block and
copying the shared one into it (kv_cache_block_copies ->
copy_kv_cache_blocks_inplace over the runner's kv_caches). With
VLLM_QSA_KV_OFFLOAD=1 a QSA layer's kv_caches entry is only the 1-byte GPU
slot per token; the real K/V lives in the pinned host pool made in
bind_kv_cache, which nothing copied. The new block kept its previous owner's
K/V. (The DeltaNet side was never the problem: MambaManager stores the
partial-tail checkpoint and copies it through the same list.)

Fix: copy_kv_cache_blocks_inplace runs registered hooks after its own copies.
The GPU model runner passes, for each copy target, the layer names of the KV
cache group that owns it. QSA registers a hook that copies a layer's host
blocks only for targets in its own group, block by block inside the mapped
host pool, and drops the decode row cache (keyed by physical slot).

rev 2: rev 1 gathered every pair through a GPU temporary. One hit makes one
copy per KV cache group (~13 here, mostly mamba), so three concurrent hits
asked for 726 MiB on a full GPU and killed the engine (MTP slug, bf16 KV).

Port for the MTP + FP8-KV tree: applies on top of local-03
(flash-next-vllm-mtp:v030-fp8kv). Same change as the fp8kv copy, context differs.

diff --git a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py
index 5911e7f..e5b3c84 100644
--- a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py
+++ b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py
@@ -248,6 +248,68 @@ def _qsa_pin_host_pool(
     return host, buf
 
 
+# Host K/V views (UVA) of the QSA layers on this rank, by layer name.
+_QSA_HOST_KV_VIEWS: dict[str, torch.Tensor] = {}
+_QSA_COW_UNMAPPED_WARNED = False
+
+
+def _qsa_copy_host_kv_blocks(indices_np, num_blocks: int, dst_block_layers=None) -> None:
+    """Copy-on-write for host-resident K/V.
+
+    A prefix-cache hit that ends inside a block (--prefix-match-unit finer than
+    the QSA block) gives the request a fresh block and asks the worker to copy
+    the shared block into it. The generic copy only sees the GPU tensors in
+    kv_caches; with VLLM_QSA_KV_OFFLOAD=1 those hold a 1-byte slot per token
+    and the real K/V stays in pinned host memory. Without this the new block
+    keeps a previous owner's K/V and the request attends to garbage.
+
+    One hit makes one copy per KV cache group, most of them for mamba groups,
+    so a layer copies only the pairs whose target block belongs to its own
+    group (dst_block_layers). A target the caller could not map is copied
+    anyway. Each pair is one block-to-block copy inside the mapped host pool:
+    no GPU temporary (a batched gather of ~40 bf16 blocks needed 726 MiB and
+    ran a full GPU out of memory). The copies run on the current stream, after
+    earlier K/V writes and before this step's forward reads the blocks.
+    """
+    global _QSA_COW_UNMAPPED_WARNED
+    if not _QSA_HOST_KV_VIEWS:
+        return
+    from .ops.qsa import _QSA_ROW_CACHES
+
+    pairs = [(int(src), int(dst)) for src, dst in indices_np]
+    devices = set()
+    for name, view in _QSA_HOST_KV_VIEWS.items():
+        blocks = None
+        for src, dst in pairs:
+            if dst_block_layers is not None:
+                layers = dst_block_layers.get(dst)
+                if layers is None:
+                    if not _QSA_COW_UNMAPPED_WARNED:
+                        _QSA_COW_UNMAPPED_WARNED = True
+                        from vllm.logger import init_logger
+
+                        init_logger(__name__).warning(
+                            "QSA host KV copy-on-write: block %d has no KV cache "
+                            "group in this step's block ids; copying it anyway.",
+                            dst,
+                        )
+                elif name not in layers:
+                    continue
+            if blocks is None:
+                # Bytes, so FP8 K/V needs no float8 kernels.
+                blocks = view.view(torch.uint8).view(num_blocks, -1)
+            blocks[dst].copy_(blocks[src])
+        if blocks is not None:
+            devices.add(view.device)
+    if not devices:
+        return
+    # The decode row cache is keyed by physical slot; rows it holds for the
+    # destination blocks belong to their previous owner.
+    for row_cache in _QSA_ROW_CACHES.values():
+        if row_cache.tags.device in devices:
+            row_cache.invalidate_all()
+
+
